  },
  "description": "HABGAW crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group I 2/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C63 H81 N12 O39 Tb7,6(C2 H3 N1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 5 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.557-3.869 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.03-117.28°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb14(L1)6(μ3-OH)12(μ2-OH)6(NO3)12]·15CH3CN·2CH3OH·4H2O (anal. C150H214N36O80Tb14). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 12 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 12 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 12 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
